WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.995
Authentication verifies identity claims for users, services, devices, applications, and workloads.

2
00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:15.023
It is different from identification, authorization, and accounting, and confusing those ideas leads to weak designs.

3
00:00:15.023 --> 00:00:18.520
Login success should never imply unlimited access.

4
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:25.356
Authentication establishes who or what is present; authorization decides what that identity may do.

5
00:00:25.356 --> 00:00:39.266
Strong authentication combines appropriate authenticators, credential protection, MFA, secure sessions, recovery controls, lifecycle management, federation governance, monitoring, and response.

6
00:00:39.266 --> 00:00:45.228
Passwords still require careful storage, reset, throttling, and usability decisions.

7
00:00:45.228 --> 00:00:53.971
MFA improves assurance, especially when phishing-resistant methods are used, but it depends on secure enrollment and recovery.

8
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:57.389
Sessions and tokens must be protected after login.

9
00:00:57.389 --> 00:01:05.179
Modern identity often involves federation, SSO, service accounts, customer identities, devices, and workloads.

10
00:01:05.179 --> 00:01:12.889
Central identity providers can improve consistency, but misconfiguration can affect many applications at once.

11
00:01:12.889 --> 00:01:21.315
Service accounts may have persistent access without a human present, so ownership, scope, rotation, and monitoring matter.

12
00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:26.243
Authentication design must cover both people and non-human identities.

13
00:01:26.243 --> 00:01:32.443
The goal is identity assurance that is secure, usable, observable, and appropriate to risk.

14
00:01:32.443 --> 00:01:35.622
Users should be able to authenticate reliably.

15
00:01:35.622 --> 00:01:39.358
Operators should be able to detect and respond to abuse.

16
00:01:39.358 --> 00:01:44.604
Security teams should be able to govern recovery, lifecycle, and federation.

17
00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:49.771
Authentication is not a single login screen; it is an ongoing system of trust.
